{%- comment -%}
  Add-to-cart recipe. Facts this encodes:
  - Prefer the product: option with the selected product drop.
  - A VARIANT IS A PRODUCT — to sell a specific variant, submit that variant
    product as the form target. There is no variant_id field on the form.
  - Gate with can_add_to_cart? / out_of_stock? (there is no product.available).
  - price field only for variable-pricing products; booking fields for bookables.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% default product: nil %}

{% if product.out_of_stock? %}
  <p class="stock-message">{{ product.out_of_stock_text }}</p>
{% elsif product.available_only_in_bundle? %}
  <p class="stock-message">{{ product.unavailable_text }}</p>
{% elsif product.can_add_to_cart? %}
  {% form "add-to-cart", product: product, class: "add-to-cart" %}
    {% render "form_errors", errors: form.errors %}

    {% if product.can_select_quantity? %}
      <label for="atc-qty">{{ "products.show.quantity" | t }}</label>
      <input type="number" id="atc-qty" name="{{ form.quantity.name }}"
             value="1" min="1"
             {% if product.maximum_quantity %}max="{{ product.maximum_quantity }}"{% endif %}>
    {% endif %}

    <button type="submit">{{ product.add_to_cart_text | default: "products.show.add_to_cart" | t }}</button>
  {% endform %}
{% endif %}

{%- comment -%}
  Variant selection: render one control per variant type; each choice maps to a
  variant product. Swap the form's product to the selected variant (JS sets a
  hidden product target, or navigate to the variant's own path).

  {% for type in product.variant_types %}
    <label for="{{ type.form_value }}">{{ type.name }}</label>
    <select id="{{ type.form_value }}" name="{{ type.form_value }}">
      {% for choice in type.variant_choices %}
        <option value="{{ choice.value }}">{{ choice.label }}</option>
      {% endfor %}
    </select>
  {% endfor %}
{%- endcomment -%}
